      "boundaryDescription": "No worded boundary is published. The council's public notice states only that 'The areas are detailed on plans accompanying the Designations'; the signed designation PDF for this area is a scanned plan. Use the street/postcode list plus the council's searchable map at the checkerUrl.",
      "evidence": "Union of the council's six separate s.80 designations, all made 14 Nov 2025 and in force 15 Feb 2026 to 14 Feb 2031. The council states verbatim that not all properties within a listed street or postcode are subject to licensing, because of where the boundary falls, so these lists are indicative. Street and postcode list transcribed verbatim from the council's own per-area page (heading 'Eastwood / Clifton / Boston Castle / Town Centre', sub-heading 'Proposed Roads:'), linked from the council's 'Areas Subject to Selective Licensing' page for the in-force 2026 to 2031 scheme at https://www.rotherham.gov.uk/housing/selective-licensing-2026-2031/3. 208 street/postcode rows were published, giving 111 distinct street names and 202 distinct postcodes. Two independent HTML extractions (paragraph-element parse and full-text parse) produced byte-identical row sets, so no column misalignment. The council warns verbatim: 'Please be advised that not all properties within a street or postcode may be subject to Selective Licensing due to where the boundary falls, so please check individual addresses using the maps available above.' The signed designation PDF for this area (https://www.rotherham.gov.uk/downloads/file/4762/town-centre-eastwood-clifton-boston-castle-designation) is a scanned image with no extractable text and carries only a plan, so no house-number schedule exists to transcribe; numbers are therefore null for every street and a street match must be treated as 'likely, confirm on the council map' rather than certain.",
      "listIsIndicative": true
